{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/100710","id":2248124765,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6F_6ld","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100710","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100710.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100710.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100710","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/100710/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/100710/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100710/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/00a9b9b5063c3d7b8cbe872d6f95824acb4f63a8","number":100710,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Expose light storage to render data","user":{"login":"BadMachine","id":50546204,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNTQ2MjA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50546204?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BadMachine","html_url":"https://github.com/BadMachine","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BadMachine/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BadMachine/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BadMachine/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BadMachine/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BadMachine/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BadMachine/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BadMachine/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BadMachine/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BadMachine/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This pull request adds functionality that allows access to the LightStorage object via the RenderData object. This enhances the ability to work with lighting data during rendering, providing new methods to retrieve light buffers.\r\n\r\n1. omni_light_buffer – a buffer for processing omni-lights (lights emitting in all directions).\r\n2. directional_light_buffer – a buffer for processing directional lights (e.g., sunlight), where light is emitted in one direction.\r\n\r\nNow, through the RenderData object, you can access the LightStorage object, and then use methods to extract the necessary light buffers for further processing in shaders or other parts of rendering.\r\n\r\nExample usage:\r\n```gdscript\r\nfunc _render_callback(p_effect_callback_type, p_render_data: RenderData):\r\n    var light_storage: LightStorage = p_render_data.get_light_storage()\r\n\r\n    var directional_light_buffer: RID = light_storage.get_directional_light_buffer()\r\n    var omni_light_buffer: RID = light_storage.get_omni_light_buffer()\r\n    var spot_light_buffer: RID = light_storage.get_spot_light_buffer()\r\n    \r\n    var texture_storage: TextureStorage = p_render_data.get_texture_storage()\r\n    var decal_atlas = texture_storage.decal_atlas_get_texture()\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis enhancement improves the flexibility of working with lighting data, allowing manipulation of light source data in compute shaders, which opens up additional opportunities for optimizing and processing light at a low level within compute shaders.","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098111,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgxMTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:rendering","name":"topic:rendering","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666708289,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4Mjg5","url